# In-flight work guard

**Invariant:** `dispatch_active(work) ∧ overlap(in_seat_work, work) ⇒ halt(in_seat)` ·
`¬abort(session) ∧ ¬cancel(dispatch) ∧ ¬kill(execution)` — unless the operator **names** the override
("abort the dispatch", "cancel 6488", "implement in IDE, don't wait for SDK"). Tier change, urgency,
slow polls, "session looked stale", and CHECKPOINT next-step changes are **not** authorization.

Active = `execution_id` / `dispatch_id` returned and not terminal · `poll_hint` open for `from_agent=cursor-sdk` ·
thread shows admit without terminal closeout · scoreboard marks the slice IN FLIGHT. Overlap = same **work
identity** (`work_key` = `todo:{slug}`; `source_ref` fallback — conductor rows carry none), `packet_path`, or
`files_expected` loci; the live conductor `dispatch_id` is the **holder** named in the 409, not the key. Lane B
worktrees do not lift the guard on the same paths.

## Forbidden / Permitted

Do not edit paths the dispatch owns or "head start while SDK runs" — poll `agent_bus.wait`, read the thread, harvest the closeout; edits stay **outside** the overlap.
Do not cancel queued cursor-sdk "as cleanup" or tear down a converse lane / live CSE — author the packet **before** firing; lead verify **after** terminal closeout.
Do not infer "no active CDP" from empty `active_work` while the private request lane runs — read that thread; transport idle ≠ bus idle.
Do not hop, re-stream, or refuse PARK to "keep the tab alive" — PARK; tab ⟂ session.
Closing an agent-bus thread ≠ aborting substrate work. Abort of a transport handle ≢ abort of the operator-proxy arc (commission lives on the private request lane). Dead `execution_id` is not reopenable — continuity is the request thread; `cse_session(op=followup)` may reattach.
